\f0\fs28\b Use-Case Flow Specification\b0\fs22\line
\fs24\b Use Case: Redeem Gift Card\b0\fs22\line
Primary Actor: Account Holder\line
Supporting Actors: System (voucher/ledger engine), Merchant Partner (receives redemption notice)\line\line

\b Preconditions\b0\line
1. The Account Holder is logged into the wallet app.\line
2. The Account Holder's exchange credit balance is greater than zero.\line\line

\b Postconditions (on success)\b0\line
1. A single-use voucher code has been generated and delivered to the Account Holder's wallet.\line
2. The Account Holder's credit balance has been debited by the gift card's value.\line
3. The voucher is locked against reuse and the issuing Merchant Partner has been notified of the redemption.\line\line

\b Main Success Scenario\b0\line
1. Account Holder opens a Merchant Partner's gift card catalogue in the app.\line
2. Account Holder selects a gift card denomination and confirms the redemption.\line
3. System checks that the Account Holder's exchange credit balance covers the gift card's value.\line
4. System deducts the required credits and generates a single-use voucher code with a cryptographic checksum.\line
5. System locks the voucher via \i Lock Voucher\i0  («include») so it cannot be redeemed a second time.\line
6. System delivers the voucher code to the Account Holder's wallet.\line
7. System notifies the Merchant Partner of the redemption via \i Notify Merchant\i0  («include»), including the voucher ID and timestamp.\line
8. Use case ends successfully.\line\line

\b Alternate Flow \endash  3a. Insufficient Credit Balance\b0\line
3a1. System detects that the Account Holder's credit balance is less than the gift card's value.\line
3a2. System displays an "insufficient balance" message and suggests converting more loyalty points.\line
3a3. Account Holder either converts more points and retries from step 2, or cancels the redemption. If cancelled, no credits are deducted and the use case ends without a voucher being issued.\line
}
